This license covers the application source code (HTML, CSS, JavaScript,
build/deploy configuration) in this repository.

The dataset in `data/collections.json` — the curated index of oral-history
and voice-testimony archive collections — is licensed separately under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This split is deliberate: the code is a tool, freely reusable under standard
open-source terms; the dataset is a curated body of factual, citable
information about third-party archives, better served by an attribution
license that keeps it easy to reuse in research while crediting the project
that compiled it. Note that CC BY 4.0 applies to this project's own
compilation and descriptions — it does not grant any rights to the
underlying archival recordings, testimonies, or materials themselves, which
remain the property of their respective holding institutions and are subject
to those institutions' own terms of access.
